# Population

A population is the complete set of individuals, objects, or observations that are of interest in a study. It includes every member of the group from which information is collected.
example of population -1. Population in a School Study
Population: All students enrolled in a school.
Purpose: To determine the average marks of all students.
2. Population in Market Research
Population: All consumers living in a city.
Purpose: To understand consumer purchasing behaviour.
3. Population in a Medical Study
Population: All patients with a specific disease.
Purpose: To study the effectiveness of a drug.
4. Population in an Election Survey
Population: All eligible voters in a state.
Purpose: To predict election results.
5. Population in an Employee Survey
Population: All employees working in a company.
Purpose: To measure employee satisfaction.
. Population in Agricultural Research
Population: All farms in a district.
Purpose: To estimate crop production.

Simple definition to remember:

Population = Entire group you want to study.

For example:

All students in a school → Population
All customers of a bank → Population
All patients in a hospital → Population
  
# Sample

A sample is a subset of the population selected to represent the entire population. Sampling involves choosing a group of individuals or observations from the population to draw conclusions about the whole population.
example of sample-1. Sample in a School Study
Sample: 50 students selected from a school.
Purpose: To estimate the average marks of all students.
2. Sample in Market Research
Sample: 500 consumers selected from a city.
Purpose: To understand the purchasing behaviour of all consumers.
3. Sample in a Medical Study
Sample: 200 patients with a specific disease.
Purpose: To test the effectiveness of a new drug.
4. Sample in an Election Survey
Sample: 1,000 voters selected from a state.
Purpose: To predict the election results.
5. Sample in an Employee Survey
Sample: 100 employees selected from a company.
Purpose: To measure employee satisfaction.
6. Sample in Agricultural Research
Sample: 50 farms selected from a district.
Purpose: To estimate crop production.
Easy Trick to Remember
Population = Entire Group
Example: All students in a school.
Sample = Small Part of the Population
Example: 50 students selected from that school.
